@title Cold Room B temperature alarm
@subtitle Marlowe Vaccine Depot runbook
@author Depot Operations

kpi Safe range | 2 to 8 °C | Cold Room B | good
kpi Stock held | 12,400 doses | must stay in range | neutral
kpi Critical | above 12 °C or below 0 °C | act now | bad

!!! Nobody discards anything. Only the Quality Manager decides what happens to any dose.

# Alarm levels
- Warning: the temperature is above 8 °C for 10 minutes.
- Critical: the temperature is above 12 °C or below 0 °C.

# First 15 minutes
1. Acknowledge the alarm on the monitoring panel within 5 minutes.
2. Check that the door is fully shut and the seal is intact.
3. Check that the compressor has power. Note the temperature shown on the data logger.
4. Call Polar Service on 555-0190. They respond within 4 hours.

# Moving stock
If the temperature is still above 8 °C after 15 minutes, move the doses to backup Cold Room C, which holds 9,000 doses.

The remaining 3,400 doses go into the 6 validated transport boxes with ice packs. Log every box on the transfer sheet.

# Quarantine and escalation
!!! Nobody discards anything. Only the Quality Manager decides.

- Any lot that is out of range for more than 30 minutes in total is quarantined.
- Tell the Quality Manager immediately.
- If the alarm is not resolved within 2 hours, call the Operations Director.

# Contacts
